  "description": "Dashboard for the Temporal Self-Hosting Workshop benchmark exercises. Helps identify performance bottlenecks and calculate theoretical throughput.",
  "editable": true,
  "fiscalYearStartMonth": 0,
  "graphTooltip": 0,
  "id": null,
  "links": [],
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 900,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "How to Read This Dashboard",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Pick your cluster with `$cluster`** (top left, defaults to cluster-1) -- unlike the Bitovi Temporal Dashboard, this variable has no \"All\" option, since blending two clusters' shard/throughput numbers together defeats the point of a benchmarking exercise.\n\n**Top row** (Shard Utilization, Persistence Latency p95, History CPU, Theoretical Max Throughput) is the always-visible summary. The rows below match the workshop exercises:\n- *Exercise 1: Shard-Based Throughput* -- calculate the theoretical ceiling from persistence latency and live shard count.\n- *Exercise 2: Actual Workflow Throughput* -- what you're actually driving, to compare against the theoretical number above.\n- *Exercise 3: History Service Resources* -- is the History service itself the constraint.\n- *Exercise 5: Bottleneck Identification* -- the key diagnostic: if History latency >> Persistence latency with low DB CPU, that's shard contention; if the two are close with high DB CPU, that's a database bottleneck.\n\nShard-count-dependent formulas (Shard Utilization %, Theoretical Max Throughput, Workflows Per Shard Per Second) now read the live shard count from `numshards_gauge` for whichever cluster `$cluster` selects, instead of a hardcoded number -- they stay correct even if you change the Helm values' shard count."
      }
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "TemporalMetrics"
      },
      "description": "Percentage of theoretical shard capacity being used. < 50% is healthy. Shard count is now read live from numshards_gauge for the selected $cluster instead of a hardcoded number -- no more editing this formula when shard count differs.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "mappings": [],
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 50
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 80
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "percent",
          "noValue": "0"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 6
      },
      "id": 2,
      "options": {
        "minVizHeight": 75,
        "minVizWidth": 75,
        "orientation": "auto",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "showThresholdLabels": false,
        "showThresholdMarkers": true,
        "sizing": "auto",
        "text": {}
      },
      "pluginVersion": "11.0.0",
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "TemporalMetrics"
          },
          "expr": "(sum(rate(service_requests{app_kubernetes_io_instance=\"$cluster\",operation=\"StartWorkflowExecution\",service_name=\"frontend\"}[5m])) / scalar(max(numshards_gauge{app_kubernetes_io_instance=\"$cluster\",app_kubernetes_io_instance=\"$cluster\"}))) / (1000 / histogram_quantile(0.50, sum(rate(persistence_latency_bucket{app_kubernetes_io_instance=\"$cluster\",service_name=\"history\"}[5m])) by (le))) * 100",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Shard Utilization %",
      "type": "gauge"
